(LST-67 — the position-loop guard idiom (LANGUAGE.md:2664-2676, the fix
 Discrepancy 3 called for): the predicate reads the runtime tag but does not
 narrow the static type, so `item add 1` on a `For each` loop variable is
 still refused inside the guard (see D3.vox). Getting the guarded element
 into a DECLARED variable via a position loop, instead, lets arithmetic run.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST-67.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   12
   guarded away
   guarded away
)
a list called mixedbag is [11, "two", 3.5].
For each position from 1 to mixedbag's length,
  if element position of mixedbag is a number,
    a number called got is element position of mixedbag,
    print got add 1.
  otherwise print "guarded away".
